- rospy.spin() might be the key to exiting the process once the program finishes running
- The publisher node is called chatter and then the subscriber subscribed to this named node (ex2p1.2)
When you create a topic in ros, messages are exchanged between nodes, but the message type must be a single type of message (string, JPEG image, etc)

Seems to be a helpful link to understand how to do wheel odometry with duckiebots specifically: https://docs-old.duckietown.org/daffy/duckietown-robotics-development/out/odometry_modeling.html
-- It shows that distance travelled by robot, x
x = 2 * pi * R * (N_ticks / N_total)
N_total for our duckiebot is 135
N_ticks gotten via subscribing to the encoder reader topic
R can be achieved by getting the parameter for kinematics_node/radius topic. Remember that we even set the trim param, and were able to see the radius as one of the params